      "claim": "Ketanserin absolute bioavailability was 55.5 ± 8.7% after a 60 mg oral dose in healthy male subjects, supporting F >= 20%.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "All retrieved evidence molecules with numeric or clearly affirmative bioavailability data report oral F values well above 20%, including multiple absolute bioavailability measurements in humans. No affirmative evidence for F < 20% was provided.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "Molecule 1 contains records for different opioids (morphine/methadone vs meperidine/pethidine); inconsistent cards were discounted, but the consistent meperidine/pethidine records still support high bioavailability.",
    "Some records are qualitative (e.g., 'excellent', 'low') rather than numeric absolute F; numeric absolute measurements were prioritized.",
    "No retrieved evidence directly supports F < 20% for any molecule."
  ],
